{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a2a41815",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Saved-data plots and descriptive analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Select **Python (search_decimation)** and set `CONFIG_PATH` and `RUN_PATHS`.\n",
    "Paths select existing saved runs; no simulation or decoding is performed.\n",
    "Validation/loading, failure summaries, timing summaries and plotting have separate\n",
    "cells. Rerun the plotting cell to redraw without reading the data again.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook uses output, confidence, quantiles, plots, timing stratification and\n",
    "tail-support settings from `analysis`. Bootstrap and accuracy-margin settings are\n",
    "used only by the separate full-report CLI, not by this notebook.\n",
    "Run/scientific/decoder/execution groups stay separate, including replay trials.\n",
    "BB uses one physical block trial per shot with all 12 logical Z observables."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "790b50ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import analysis\n",
    "# Select Python (search_decimation), restart, then run all cells.\n",
    "# The CLI injects CONFIG_PATH/RUN_PATHS; interactive users may edit them first.\n",
    "ROOT = next((p for p in (Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents) if (p / \"pyproject.toml\").is_file()), Path.cwd())\n",
    "CONFIG_PATH = globals().get(\"CONFIG_PATH\", os.environ.get(\"QEC_ANALYSIS_CONFIG\", str(ROOT / \"config/analysis.yaml.example\")))\n",
    "RUN_PATHS = globals().get(\"RUN_PATHS\", [os.environ[\"QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN\"]] if \"QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN\" in os.environ else [])\n",
    "if not hasattr(analysis, \"load_analysis_config\") or not hasattr(analysis, \"analysis_runtime\"):\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(f\"Old analysis package: {analysis.__file__}; Python: {sys.executable}. Select Python (search_decimation), restart the kernel, and run all cells.\")\n",
    "if (ROOT / \"analysis\").is_dir() and Path(analysis.__file__).resolve().parent != (ROOT / \"analysis\").resolve():\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(f\"Analysis loaded from another checkout: {analysis.__file__}; Python: {sys.executable}. Select this workspace's search_decimation environment and restart the kernel.\")\n",
    "runtime = analysis.analysis_runtime()\n",
    "if (ROOT / \"src/qec_bp_benchmark/config.py\").is_file() and Path(runtime[\"config_path\"]) != (ROOT / \"src/qec_bp_benchmark/config.py\").resolve():\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(f\"Configuration package loaded from another checkout: {runtime['config_path']}; Python: {sys.executable}. Select this workspace's search_decimation environment and restart the kernel.\")\n",
    "if not RUN_PATHS:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Select saved run paths explicitly in RUN_PATHS or QEC_ANALYSIS_RUN\")\n",
    "from analysis import load_analysis_config, analysis_runtime\n",
    "config = load_analysis_config(CONFIG_PATH)\n",
    "import matplotlib\n",
    "matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n",
    "analysis_runtime()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9325740a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load and validate saved data once\n",
    "\n",
    "Checks manifests, shard checksums, counts and identities. This can take time for\n",
    "large runs and materializes the data in memory. Subsequent cells reuse `records`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "eba389cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from analysis.io import load_run, select_records\n",
    "\n",
    "runs = []\n",
    "for path in RUN_PATHS:\n",
    "    print(f\"Validating saved run: {path}\", flush=True)\n",
    "    runs.append(load_run(path))\n",
    "records = select_records(runs)\n",
    "if not records:\n",
    "    raise ValueError(\"Selection contains no committed decode rows\")\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(records):,} decode records from {len(runs)} runs\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3b762531",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Failure rates\n",
    "\n",
    "Block failure includes decoding failure or any valid logical mismatch. Component\n",
    "rates use all physical shots; conditional mismatch uses only valid outputs.\n",
    "Wilson intervals use physical shots, not observable bits. Zero-event triangles\n",
    "in plots mark the Wilson upper bound, not a positive estimated failure rate."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8e46b060",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from analysis.statistics import aggregate_failures\n",
    "\n",
    "failures = aggregate_failures(records, confidence=config.analysis.confidence)\n",
    "[(row[\"family\"], row[\"distance\"], row[\"decoder_name\"], row[\"shots\"], row[\"block_failure\"])\n",
    " for row in failures]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f35d523d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Measured execution times\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses saved complete-block CPU/wall durations, including failed shots, without\n",
    "normalizing by rounds or observables. Isolated/concurrent contexts stay separate.\n",
    "Quantiles retain sample counts, expected tail counts and insufficient-tail flags."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5c3f858f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from analysis.statistics import aggregate_timings\n",
    "\n",
    "timings = aggregate_timings(\n",
    "    records, quantiles=config.analysis.quantiles,\n",
    "    stratify=config.analysis.stratify_timing,\n",
    "    min_expected_tail_count=config.analysis.min_expected_tail_count,\n",
    ")\n",
    "[(r[\"family\"], r[\"distance\"], r[\"decoder_name\"], r[\"timing_mode\"], r[\"timer\"],\n",
    "  r[\"samples\"], r[\"mean_ns\"], r[\"p99_ns\"], r[\"quantiles\"][-1]) for r in timings]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b4d5d41",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Draw selected figures\n",
    "\n",
    "Exports the configured failure-rate and CPU/wall ECDF/survival plots as PNG/PDF\n",
    "into a new directory on each execution. No hybrid stage or paired comparison\n",
    "analysis is performed. `records`, `failures` and `timings` remain available for\n",
    "further analysis through the reusable `analysis` APIs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9b01465d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from uuid import uuid4\n",
    "from IPython.display import Image, display\n",
    "from analysis.plots import plot_failure_rates, plot_timings\n",
    "\n",
    "figure_output = Path(config.analysis.output) / f\"notebook_plots_{uuid4().hex}\"\n",
    "figure_output.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=False)\n",
    "figures = []\n",
    "for plot in config.analysis.plots:\n",
    "    print(f\"Plotting {plot}\", flush=True)\n",
    "    if plot == \"failure_rate\":\n",
    "        figures.extend(plot_failure_rates(failures, figure_output))\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        figures.extend(plot_timings(\n",
    "            records, figure_output,\n",
    "            timer=\"cpu_ns\" if plot.startswith(\"cpu_\") else \"wall_ns\",\n",
    "            survival=plot.endswith(\"survival\"),\n",
    "            stratify=config.analysis.stratify_timing,\n",
    "            min_expected_tail_count=config.analysis.min_expected_tail_count,\n",
    "        ))\n",
    "print(f\"Figure directory: {figure_output}\")\n",
    "for figure in figures:\n",
    "    if figure.suffix == \".png\":\n",
    "        display(Image(filename=str(figure)))"
   ]
  }
 ],
